          "en": "Supreme People's Procuratorate of the People's Republic of China\nANNOUNCEMENT\nThe Reply of the Supreme People's Procuratorate on Issues Concerning the Application of Law to the Act of a Notary Issuing a Notarial Certificate with Major Inaccuracies was adopted at the 7th meeting of the Eleventh Procuratorial Committee of the Supreme People's Procuratorate on 6 January 2009, and is hereby promulgated and shall come into force on 15 January 2009.\nSupreme People's Procuratorate\n7 January 2009\nReply of the Supreme People's Procuratorate on Issues Concerning the Application of Law to the Act of a Notary\nIssuing a Notarial Certificate with Major Inaccuracies\n(Adopted at the 7th meeting of the Eleventh Procuratorial Committee\nof the Supreme People's Procuratorate on 6 January 2009)\nGao Jian Fa Shi Zi No. 1 [2009]\nTo the People's Procuratorate of Gansu Province:\nYour procuratorate's request for instructions, Gan Jian Fa Yan No. 17 [2008], on whether a notary's issuance of a certification document with major inaccuracies constitutes a crime, has been received. After study, the following reply is given:\nAfter the Notarisation Law of the People's Republic of China came into force, where a notary, in the course of performing his notarial duties, is seriously irresponsible and the notarial certificate issued by him contains major inaccuracies, thereby causing serious consequences, he shall, in accordance with paragraph 3 of Article 229 of the Criminal Law, be investigated for criminal responsibility for the crime of issuing certificates with major inaccuracies.\nThis is our reply.\nSupreme People's Procuratorate\n7 January 2009"
