        "text": {
          "en": "Supreme People's Procuratorate of the People's Republic of China\nANNOUNCEMENT\nThe Reply of the Supreme People's Procuratorate on the Request for Instructions Concerning Whether a State Functionary's Misappropriation of Non-Specific Public Property May Be Convicted was adopted at the 57th meeting of the Ninth Procuratorial Committee of the Supreme People's Procuratorate on 6 March 2000, and is hereby promulgated and shall come into force on 15 March 2000.\nSupreme People's Procuratorate\n15 March 2000\nReply of the Supreme People's Procuratorate on the Request for Instructions Concerning Whether\na State Functionary's Misappropriation of Non-Specific Public Property May Be Convicted\n(Adopted at the 57th meeting of the Ninth Procuratorial Committee\nof the Supreme People's Procuratorate on 6 March 2000)\nGao Jian Fa Shi Zi No. 1 [2000]\nTo the People's Procuratorate of Shandong Province:\nYour procuratorate's request for instructions, Lu Jian Fa Yan Zi No. 3 [1999], on whether a State functionary's misappropriation of non-specific public property may be convicted, has been received. After study, it is considered that the crime of misappropriating public funds prescribed in Article 384 of the Criminal Law does not include the act of misappropriating non-specific public property for personal use, and such an act shall not be treated as the crime of misappropriating public funds. If it constitutes another crime, it shall be convicted and punished in accordance with the relevant provisions of the Criminal Law.\nThis is our reply.\nSupreme People's Procuratorate\n15 March 2000"
        },
